  "bedrock": {
    "note": "Stratigraphic templates, youngest unit first. A column starts at its subcrop unit (mapped from the subcrop tile's age names) and runs down to the basement; thicknesses are scaled to fit basement depth minus the cover. A subcrop entry may name a 'start' layer; otherwise the column starts at the first layer of the unit whose 'lith' matches the subcrop_lith tile (younger layers taken as eroded). 'basement' as a unit means the basement comes straight under the cover. 'fadeLon' thins a unit from full at the first longitude to nothing at the second (the Silurian is 610 m at Ventspils, 455 m at Ruhnu, a few metres at Valga). Thicknesses: LVGMC Riga/Daugavpils/Ventspils reports, Ruhnu and Valga boreholes (baltic-real-columns.md).",
